*Re: Application — Backend Java Developer*

#v(0.5em)

Dear Hiring Team,

I'm applying for backend Java developer positions. I have 20+ years of experience, with a particular focus on financial applications: I led and built backend systems at Banco Credicoop (GUV system — check validation, batch/ETL processes, and APIs on the banking core), Baufest for BBVA (migrating analog banking processes to REST microservices), Banco Industrial SA, AstroPay (end-to-end integration of a new bank as PSP for CVU operations and account-to-account transfers), and ERON International, where I built and maintained payment integrations with more than ten LATAM providers on a Java/Spring Boot microservices platform on AWS. I work daily with Spring Boot, RESTful API design, relational and non-relational databases, and Git, and completed a DevOps Diploma (UNC, 2024).

Beyond that technical depth, in parallel I design, build, and run TuFactura in production, my own invoicing SaaS, where I'm the sole owner end-to-end — from API design to deployment and support. That real ownership experience — taking a problem, solving it, and keeping it running in production without waiting for it to be "someone else's job" — is the same autonomy and commitment to outcomes I look to bring to a new team.

I live in Buenos Aires and location or work format isn't a constraint for me — remote, hybrid, or on-site all work.

I'm looking for a long-term role where I can keep building and owning outcomes, and I'd welcome the chance to talk about how my backend Java experience in the financial sector could contribute to your team. Thank you for your consideration.

Best regards,

Jonathan Museri

